\f0\b \ul Evalution metrics:
\f1\b0 \ulnone \

\f0\b \ul Accuracy
\f1\b0 \ulnone : overall correctness, total number of true classifications divided by total number of classifications\
		Accuracy = TP + TN / Total number of classifications\

\f0\b \ul Recall /sensitivity: 
\f1\b0 \ulnone how many actual positives were identified\
		Recall TP/TP + FN\

\f0\b \ul Precision:
\f1\b0 \ulnone  how many predicted positives are correct\
		Precision= TP/TP+ FP\

\f0\b \ul F1 score:
\f1\b0 \ulnone  balance between precision and recall\
		F1= 2(precision * recall)/precision+ recall\

\f0\b \ul Specificity:
\f1\b0 \ulnone  measures how well negative are identified\
		Specificity = TN/TN+ FP\

\f0\b \ul ROC curve (receiver operation characteristic):
\f1\b0 \ulnone  Used to determine the best threshold value\

\f0\b \ul AUC curve (Area Under Curve):
\f1\b0 \ulnone  use it to determine the best model the model which covers the maximum area under the curve is \
considered as the best model\
\
